   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tunnel Portal Aesthetics</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Tunnel Portal Aesthetics: Nine Orthogonal Design Schemes\",\n  \"description\": \"Method replication with the paper's own renderings: participants approach nine 3D-modelled design schemes for the same motorway headwall tunnel portal (Banlun Tunnel) and grade the aesthetics of each on the paper's five-level comment set (great, good, ordinary, relatively bad, bad), quickly and by first impression. The nine schemes are the paper's L9(3^4) orthogonal design crossing portal line (straight, step type, arch), colour (blue, green, concrete), greening (delicate, simple, none) and texture (mural, simple treatment, none). As in the paper, everyone grades all nine twice: a first round, then, once familiar with all nine, a second round. Rebuilt from Ye, Su, Wei, Xu & Liang (2020), PLOS ONE 15(9): e0238762, with the renderings printed in its Fig 10 (CC BY 4.0). Analysis as in the paper: count the grades per scheme, normalise to a membership vector and multiply by the evaluation set {95, 85, 75, 65, 60} to get each scheme's aesthetic score; then range analysis over the orthogonal table (mean score at each level of each factor; the factor with the largest range matters most) to pick the best level of each factor. Differences from the original study: (1) the original used a driving simulator (Euro Truck Simulator 2, up to 80 km/h) with participants driving through each portal; here each approach is a 7 s zoom into the published rendering, so there is no real motion, steering or traffic; (2) the renderings are cropped from the published figure (about 640 x 320 px); (3) the original drivers rested about 10 min after each portal; here there is no rest; (4) the paper does not report the presentation order; here each round uses a new random order, and before round 2 the nine schemes are shown side by side so that participants are familiar with all of them; (5) the original sample was 10 male graduate students with more than three years of driving experience; the age, gender and driving-experience questions here are our wording.\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"portals\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"start\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"inputType\": \"number\",\n      \"name\": \"age\",\n      \"title\": \"How old are you?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"min\": 18,\n      \"max\": 110\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"gender\",\n      \"title\": \"Gender\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"female\",\n        \"text\": \"Female\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"male\",\n        \"text\": \"Male\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other\",\n        \"text\": \"Other / prefer not to say\"\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"driving_years\",\n      \"title\": \"How many years of driving experience do you have?\",\n      \"description\": \"Our wording; the paper's drivers all had more than three years of experience.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"I do not drive\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"under_1\",\n        \"text\": \"Less than 1 year\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"1_3\",\n        \"text\": \"1-3 years\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"3_10\",\n        \"text\": \"More than 3 and up to 10 years\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"over_10\",\n        \"text\": \"More than 10 years\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"round1\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"aesthetic_1\",\n      \"title\": \"How beautiful was this tunnel portal?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"great\",\n        \"text\": \"Great\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"good\",\n        \"text\": \"Good\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"ordinary\",\n        \"text\": \"Ordinary\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"relatively_bad\",\n        \"text\": \"Relatively bad\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"bad\",\n        \"text\": \"Bad\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Paper's comment set (great / good / ordinary / relatively bad / bad). Round 1: first impression, right after the approach. Keyed by scheme: scheme_1 ... scheme_9 = Schemes I-IX of the paper's L9(3^4) orthogonal table (Table 2): A portal line (1-3 straight, 4-6 step type, 7-9 arch), B colour, C greening, D texture. Scoring as in the paper: great = 95, good = 85, ordinary = 75, relatively bad = 65, bad = 60; a scheme's score is the mean over all gradings (fuzzy comprehensive evaluation).\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"round2\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"aesthetic_2\",\n      \"title\": \"How beautiful was this tunnel portal?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"great\",\n        \"text\": \"Great\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"good\",\n        \"text\": \"Good\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"ordinary\",\n        \"text\": \"Ordinary\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"relatively_bad\",\n        \"text\": \"Relatively bad\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"bad\",\n        \"text\": \"Bad\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Paper's comment set (great / good / ordinary / relatively bad / bad). Round 2: after seeing all nine schemes side by side. Keyed by scheme: scheme_1 ... scheme_9 = Schemes I-IX of the paper's L9(3^4) orthogonal table (Table 2): A portal line (1-3 straight, 4-6 step type, 7-9 arch), B colour, C greening, D texture. Scoring as in the paper: great = 95, good = 85, ordinary = 75, relatively bad = 65, bad = 60; a scheme's score is the mean over all gradings (fuzzy comprehensive evaluation).\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"tunnel-original\">{\"source\": \"Ye, Su, Wei, Xu & Liang (2020) PLOS ONE 15(9): e0238762\", \"n\": 10, \"participants\": \"10 male graduate students aged 23-25 with more than three years of driving experience; driving simulator, each scheme graded in two tests (20 gradings per scheme)\", \"design_L9\": {\"scheme_1\": \"straight, blue, delicate greening, mural\", \"scheme_2\": \"straight, green, simple greening, simple treatment\", \"scheme_3\": \"straight, concrete, no greening, no texture\", \"scheme_4\": \"step, blue, simple greening, no texture\", \"scheme_5\": \"step, green, no greening, mural\", \"scheme_6\": \"step, concrete, delicate greening, simple treatment\", \"scheme_7\": \"arch, blue, no greening, simple treatment\", \"scheme_8\": \"arch, green, delicate greening, no texture\", \"scheme_9\": \"arch, concrete, simple greening, mural\"}, \"grade_counts_table3\": {\"scheme_1\": [13, 5, 2, 0, 0], \"scheme_2\": [0, 8, 7, 3, 2], \"scheme_3\": [0, 5, 12, 3, 0], \"scheme_4\": [2, 9, 7, 2, 0], \"scheme_5\": [3, 8, 7, 2, 0], \"scheme_6\": [8, 4, 6, 2, 0], \"scheme_7\": [4, 2, 10, 4, 0], \"scheme_8\": [1, 7, 7, 5, 0], \"scheme_9\": [8, 7, 5, 0, 0]}, \"scores_table4\": {\"scheme_1\": 90.5, \"scheme_2\": 76, \"scheme_3\": 76, \"scheme_4\": 80.5, \"scheme_5\": 81, \"scheme_6\": 84, \"scheme_7\": 78, \"scheme_8\": 77, \"scheme_9\": 86.5}, \"result\": \"Scheme I (straight line, blue, delicate greening, mural) scored highest (90.5) and Schemes II and III lowest (76). Range analysis ranked the factors: portal texture had the largest effect, then greening, then colour, and portal line the smallest. Best combination A2B1C1D1: step-type portal, blue mural decoration, delicate greening.\"}</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#eef2f5;--card:#fff;--ink:#1b2229;--muted:#5a6772;--accent:#1f5f8b;--line:#d5dde3;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#e2eef7}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 8px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.prog{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}\n.view{position:fixed;inset:0;background:#000;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:5;overflow:hidden}\n.win{width:min(96vw,900px);aspect-ratio:16/8;overflow:hidden;position:relative}\n.win img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;transform-origin:50% 55%;animation:drive var(--d,7s) linear forwards}\n@keyframes drive{from{transform:scale(1)}to{transform:scale(1.8)}}\n.view .t{position:absolute;bottom:12px;left:0;right:0;text-align:center;color:#999;font-size:.85rem}\n.thumb{width:100%;max-width:460px;border-radius:8px;display:block;margin:0 auto 12px}\n.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:6px}\n.grid img{width:100%;border-radius:6px;display:block}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer}\nlabel.opt:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent)}\n.f{margin-top:16px}\ninput[type=number]{font:inherit;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;width:110px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Renderings: Ye, Su, Wei, Xu &amp; Liang (2020), PLOS ONE 15(9): e0238762, Fig 10 (doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0238762, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='tunnel-portal:state', T=window.__VIEWMS?{drive:window.__VIEWMS}:{drive:7000};\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, ids=[], st=null;\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function shuffle(a){a=a.slice();for(var i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1)),t=a[i];a[i]=a[j];a[j]=t;}return a;}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function val(name){var x=app.querySelector('input[name=\"'+name+'\"]:checked');return x?x.value:null;}\n  function radios(q,nm){return '<div class=\"f\"><b>'+esc(Q[q].title)+'</b>'+(Q[q].choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+(nm||q)+'\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div>';}\n  function intro(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Tunnel portal designs</h1><p>You will \"drive\" towards nine design schemes for the same motorway tunnel portal. Each approach lasts about 7 seconds; right after it, grade how beautiful the portal looked using your first impression. After all nine you will see them side by side and grade each one a second time. It takes about 8 minutes.</p><div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');send([SPSite.answer('consent',true)],this,function(){st.step='about';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function about(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"f\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><b>'+esc(Q.age.title)+'</b><br><input type=\"number\" id=\"age\" min=\"18\" max=\"110\"></div>'+radios('gender')+radios('driving_years')+'<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Continue</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var age=Number(document.getElementById('age').value),g=val('gender'),d=val('driving_years');\n      if(!(age>=18&&age<=110))return err('Please enter your age.');if(!g||!d)return err('Please answer every question.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('age',age),SPSite.answer('gender',g),SPSite.answer('driving_years',d)],this,function(){st.step='trial';st.r=1;st.k=0;st.phase='view';save();route();});\n    };\n  }\n  function order(){return st.r===1?st.o1:st.o2;}\n  function trial(){\n    if(st.phase==='q')return rate();\n    var id=order()[st.k],v=document.createElement('div');v.className='view';\n    v.innerHTML='<div class=\"win\"><img alt=\"Approaching the tunnel portal\" style=\"--d:'+T.drive+'ms\" src=\"'+esc(files[id].url)+'\"></div><div class=\"t\">Round '+st.r+' · portal '+(st.k+1)+' of '+order().length+'</div>';\n    app.innerHTML='';app.appendChild(v);\n    setTimeout(function(){st.phase='q';save();route();},T.drive);\n  }\n  function rate(){\n    var id=order()[st.k],q='aesthetic_'+st.r;\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"prog\">Round '+st.r+' of 2 · portal '+(st.k+1)+' of '+order().length+'</div><div class=\"card\"><img class=\"thumb\" alt=\"The tunnel portal you just approached\" src=\"'+esc(files[id].url)+'\">'+radios(q,'q_grade')+'<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">'+(st.k+1<order().length?'Next portal':'Continue')+'</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var p=val('q_grade');if(p==null)return err('Please choose a grade.');\n      send([SPSite.answer(q,p,{key:id,shown:[files[id].name]})],this,function(){\n        st.k++;st.phase='view';\n        if(st.k>=order().length){if(st.r===1){st.step='between';}else st.step='done';}\n        save();route();});\n    };\n  }\n  function between(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>All nine schemes</h2><div class=\"card\"><p style=\"color:var(--ink)\">These are the nine portal designs you just saw. Take a moment to compare them. You will now approach each one again, in a new order, and grade it a second time.</p><div class=\"grid\">'+st.o1.map(function(id){return '<img alt=\"Tunnel portal scheme\" src=\"'+esc(files[id].url)+'\">';}).join('')+'</div><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start round 2</button></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){st.step='trial';st.r=2;st.k=0;st.phase='view';save();route();};\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='trial')return trial();if(s==='between')return between();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','age','gender','driving_years','aesthetic_1','aesthetic_2'].forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('portals')||[]).forEach(function(f){if(/\\.(png|jpe?g|webp)$/i.test(f.name)){var k=f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'');files[k]=f;ids.push(k);}});\n    if(ids.length<2){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload the renderings to the media folder \"portals\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var valid=st&&st.o1&&st.o1.length===ids.length&&st.o1.every(function(x){return files[x];});\n    if(!valid)st={step:'intro',o1:shuffle(ids),o2:shuffle(ids),r:1,k:0,phase:'view'};\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};if(a.consent!==true){st.step='intro';st.r=1;st.k=0;}\n    if(st.step==='trial'&&st.phase!=='q')st.phase='view';\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
